      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\), we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply the numerators**: The numerators of the fractions \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) are 1 and 3, respectively. We multiply these together:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 3 = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply the denominators**: The denominators of the fractions \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) are 5 and 7, respectively. We multiply these together:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 7 = 35\n   \\]\n\n3. **Form the new fraction**: The product of the numerators over the product of the denominators gives us the new fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1 \\times 3}{5 \\times 7} = \\frac{3}{35}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{35}}\\).",
